{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_tests_rls_deny_all_test_rls_deny_all_test", "label": "rls_deny_all_test (posture sweeps, ^ref-64)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/tests/rls_deny_all_test.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seven read-only catalogue sweeps proving the ADR-004 deny-all posture, runnable against the live project via migrations_apply_test.sh --db-url. 1a every public table has RLS on; 1b anon holds nothing on any table or view; 1c authenticated holds no write privilege; 1d a table authenticated can SELECT carries a SELECT policy; 1e anon holds EXECUTE on no function in public; 1f the seven no-grant functions (fn_audit_row, fn_audit_log_append_only, fn_stock_ledger_append_only, fn_stock_ledger_opening_closed, fn_require_lot_for_meat, fn_rollup_smoke_log_input and peers) are executable by neither role, by name; 1g every other fn_* is executable by authenticated and not by anon. FINDING that motivated ^ref-64: pg_default_acl in a Supabase project grants to anon and authenticated BY NAME, and `revoke ... from public` does not remove a named-role grant \u2014 so every revoke in the repo was real in Docker and inert live, leaving 1b/1c green over 22 open function grants. Docker has no default ACLs and structurally cannot see it."}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_tests_rls_deny_all_test_rls_deny_all_test", "target": "supabase_tests_rls_behaviour_test_rls_behaviour_test", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/rls_deny_all_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_tests_rls_deny_all_test_rls_deny_all_test", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/rls_deny_all_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_tests_rls